{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.SpectralDecompositionQvalue","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.SpectralDecompositionQvalue","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_self_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torus_knot_self_duality","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L219-L224","doc":"Self-duality: τ(r,s) ↔ τ(s,r) provides the inner product for\ncompleteness of the torus knot basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tower_terminates_at_degree_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tower_terminates_at_degree_2","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L206-L217","doc":"The jet bundle over Σ₄ has exactly three non-zero levels (k = 0, 1, 2).\nDegree 3 requires genus ≥ 13, exceeding the genus-4 bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shell_product_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shell_product_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L188-L204","doc":"**Per-shell cancellation discharged.** If every shell other than `active`\nis inactive — non-embeddable, or unchanged with nonzero parent trace — the\nshell-factor product collapses to the active shell's factor, with the\n`hInactive` hypothesis of `knot_operator_product_collapse` now *proved* for\nthis model rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellFactor_unchanged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellFactor_unchanged","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L176-L186","doc":"**Unchanged branch.** An embeddable shell left untouched by the decay\n(`daughterTrace = parentTrace`, nonzero) cancels in the ratio: `F = 1`.\nThis is the genuine \"cancels in ratio\" mechanism — `div_self`, not an\nassumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellFactor_nonembeddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellFactor_nonembeddable","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L170-L174","doc":"**Non-embeddable branch.** A non-embeddable shell contributes `F = 1`\n(definitional: it has zero action on `Σ_g`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.shellFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.shellFactor","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L162-L168","doc":"The knot-operator factor `F(τ,N)` for one shell, at the ratio level (the\ncorollary's four cases collapsed to two):\n* non-embeddable → `1` (null: zero action on `Σ_g`);\n* embeddable → the trace ratio `daughterTrace / parentTrace` (which is the\n  active shell's `tr_M` ratio, and equals `1` on an unchanged shell). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.embeddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.embeddable","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L160-L160","doc":"Whether the shell's torus knot is embeddable on `Σ_g` (else `F = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.daughterTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.daughterTrace","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L158-L158","doc":"Markov-trace weight of the shell in the daughter nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.parentTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.parentTrace","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L156-L156","doc":"Markov-trace weight of the shell in the parent nucleus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ShellState.mk","kind":"ctor","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ShellState","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ShellState","kind":"structure","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L151-L160","doc":"Per-shell decay data at the ratio level: the shell's Markov-trace weight\nbefore (parent) and after (daughter) the decay, and whether the shell's knot\nis embeddable on `Σ_g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.spectral_decomposition_qvalue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.spectral_decomposition_qvalue","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L93-L137","doc":"**Spectral decomposition of the Q_q-value** (Corollary, conditional on the\nper-shell Rosso–Jones cancellation `hInactive`).\n\nFor β⁻ decay N_{Z,N} → N_{Z+1,N-1}, the Q_q-value admits\nthe spectral decomposition:\n\n  Q_q = Q_bare × Π_{τ(r,s) ∈ E_g} F(τ(r,s), N)\n\nwhere:\n(i)   P(q) = Π V̂_j(q) is the Skein polynomial in Gröbner normal form\n(ii)  log_q is the q-natural logarithm counting exceptional divisor levels\n(iii) F(τ(r,s), N) is the knot operator (Markov trace of τ·T_β on active shells)\n(iv)  The product collapses to a single term (shell cancellation)\n(v)   The decomposition is exact — terminates at degree 2 on Σ₄\n\n**Scope (2026-11-16).** Under convention D the Pauli (fully filled shell)\nfactor `|tr_M(e_(1³)·τ·T_β·e_(1³))| / |tr_M(T_β)|` is identically `0`, since\nthe Ocneanu weight of every three-row partition vanishes at `z = q³/(q²+1)`\n(`QOU.SchurWeyl.ocneanuWeight_conventionD_eq_zero_of_three_rows`). The\ncorollary is asserted only for non-magic converting shells; this theorem is\nthe generic collapse and takes the active factor `F active` as given.\n\n**Restated 2026-08-22** (vacuity ledger, `proof-no-unused-hypothesis-rfl`).\nThe prior form `∃ Q_q, Q_q = Q_bare · knotOperator` was a trivial existential\n(`⟨rhs, rfl⟩`) that asserted nothing.  This states the `(iv)` collapse of the\nQ-value's knot-operator factor and *derives* it from the per-shell\ncancellation `hInactive` via `knot_operator_product_collapse` — the collapse\nis proved, not assumed.  The per-shell cancellation (why each inactive\n`F τ = 1`) is the Rosso–Jones content and stays the hypothesis\n(bean `qou-xq3f`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:spectral-decomposition-qvalue","label":"cor:spectral-decomposition-qvalue","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.knot_operator_product_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.knot_operator_product_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L70-L91","doc":"**Knot-operator product collapse** — the mechanism behind step `(iv)` of the\ncorollary, now *derived* rather than assumed.\n\nOver the finite embeddable torus-knot basis `E` (⊆ `E_g`), the knot-operator\nproduct `∏_{τ ∈ E} F τ` collapses to the single active shell `F active`\nwhenever every other shell contributes the identity factor `1` — non-active\nshells cancel between parent and daughter, and non-embeddable knots give\n`F = 1`.  A direct application of `Finset.prod_eq_single`.\n\nThis upgrades the earlier opaque assumption `knotOperatorProduct =\nactiveShellTerm` (a class field that *asserted* the collapse): the collapse\nof a product of mostly-`1` factors is no longer assumed but proved.  What\nremains open (bean `qou-xq3f`) is the strictly weaker *per-shell* input\n`hInactive` — that each inactive `F τ = 1`, i.e. the Rosso–Jones\ncancellation itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bareQValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bareQValue","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L64-L66","doc":"The bare Q-value: |log_q(P_dau/P_par)| · ℏ_q · m_e/3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L61-L62","doc":"The quantum Planck constant ℏ_q = (q - 1)/q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotDegree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotDegree","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L49-L59","doc":"Degree of a torus knot in the jet tower.\nDegree 1: τ(2,3), τ(2,5), τ(2,7), τ(3,5)\nDegree 2: τ(2,9), τ(3,4) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.embeddableOnBrings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.embeddableOnBrings","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L45-L47","doc":"The six nontrivial torus knots embeddable on Σ₄. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.embeddableOnSurface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.embeddableOnSurface","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L40-L43","doc":"The set of torus knot labels embeddable on Σ_g:\nE_g = {τ(r,s) : (r-1)(s-1)/2 ≤ g}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.genus","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.coprime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.coprime","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.s","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.r","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.r","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel.mk","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TorusKnotLabel","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/spectral-decomposition-qvalue.lean#L33-L38","doc":"A torus knot label τ(r, s) with coprimality and embeddability data. ","signatureChunk":0}]}